{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Teacher came to Bethany and [Bb]Martha opened wide
Her [Dm]door, her bread, her table, and the [C]fire burned inside
Her [F]sister sat at the Lord's feet and [Bb]listened to his word
While [Dm]Martha served alone and felt [C]that no one saw or heard
[Bb]Lord, don't you care that my [C]sister has left me to [Dm]serve a[Bb]lone
Tell her to help me [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Martha, Martha, [Bb]anxious over many things
[Dm]Few things are needed, [C]only one
The good [Bb]portion at his feet
[C]Will not be taken a[F]way
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Then sorrow came to Bethany, her [Bb]brother in the grave
[Dm]Four days in the tomb and [C]nothing left to save
She [F]ran to meet him on the road be[Bb]fore the others came
[Dm]Lord, if you had been here, my [C]brother would not have died
[Bb]Jesus said to her, I [C]am the resurrection and the [Dm]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Do you be[Bb]lieve this [C]
Yes, [F]Lord
[Bb]I believe that [C]you are the Christ, the [Dm]Son [C]of [Bb]God
The one coming into the [C]world
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Martha, Martha, [Bb]anxious over many things
[Dm]Few things are needed, [C]only one
